A||||5||Greg Piet||Corbeau seat installation question||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||01-28-2001||03:27 PM||||I put in a 4 point H style harness, but the stock seat does not agree well with the harness, and although I love the speakers in the headrest, I think the following seat would be better for me when I am whipping the car around the track.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.racesearch.com/CGI/racesearch_ec.cgi?race_product_id=489981;description_id=11364" TARGET=_blank>http://www.racesearch.com/CGI/racesearch_ec.cgi?race_product_id=489981;description_id=11364</A> <P>It is a corbeau brand seat with the holes in the seat for the shoulder belts to go through.  Now This seat might not be right for the Fiero, but I am currently concerned whether or not the stock Fiero seat mounts can be used in general with these type seats. <P>Does anyone have reccomendations about what seat with this style would be good for our cars?  Oh yeah plese refrain from listing $1000 seats. <P>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula 18||01-28-2001||05:03 PM||||You might want to check with Chris West. I know he sells seats I think he has mounts too. Also Trav had seats in his old 2m6. ASk him about how to ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||01-29-2001||08:36 AM||||I had Corbeau Clubmans in my car. they were just KILLER for racing but for long trips you'll kick yourself.. the Corbeau Targa RS is a MUCH more comfy seat and you'll be able to retain the harness... I've installed them in other cars..  Oh i used the stock seat slides and just drilled an extra set of holes about 2" back from the front hole and bolted up the seat. i purchased them from AUTOMOD here in Atlanta.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/corbeau.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/corbeau.jpg</A>   <P>and they retail for $320 ea! well worth the $||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||01-29-2001||08:38 AM||||oh the Forza and the clubman are the same seat just the clubman has no head restraint and like the clubman NO padding! ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||01-29-2001||12:18 PM||||Thanks for the info folks.<BR>If I am not mistaken then the stock seat bracket can be used with minimal modding to retain a Forza seat.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||01-29-2001||12:39 PM||||yep.. a few holes and a small piece of steel from you local hardware store and POOF your sittin'!||||reg||1
